Adapted from mlx_vlm/models/decider2/decider2.py: the state annotation, the
question rendering, the prompt layout and label tokens, the row batching and
padding, the per-type temperature calibration, the isolated score levels and
the shared-prefix token count.
Changes: the backbone is the mlx-lm Qwen3.5 text model rather than mlx-vlm's
qwen3_5_text, so position ids are left to that model; questions arrive as the
System One wire schema and answers are returned as raw probabilities for the
System One response builder; the packed (non-independent) scoring mode is not
included; calibration values are validated at load; the label readout rows are
materialized at construction so requests can run on worker threads.
